notice to student
When the dean or the department chair, as the case may be, has been so informed, they shall notify the student in writing accordingly, provide the student with a copy of the Code and subsequently afford the student an opportunity for discussion of the matter. The notice shall:
Include the date of the alleged offence and a brief summary of the allegation against the student;
invite the student to a meeting to discuss the matter;
inform the student that they are entitled to seek advice, or to be represented by counsel at the meeting;
include the information set out in section 19 below
specify a deadline for the student’s response to the invitation to meet;
inform the student that failure to respond by the deadline shall
At the discretion of the dean, result in a deemed admission of guilt and the imposition of one or more sanctions (all of which are to be specified in the notice), provided that the sanctions desired are within the power of the dean or chair to impose and are consistent with the Provost’s Guidelines on Sanctions; or,
